# Named `Dockerfile.dockerignore`, not `.dockerignore`: BuildKit looks for a
# per-Dockerfile ignore file beside the Dockerfile and otherwise falls back to
# one at the context root — a `.dockerignore` sitting here is silently ignored,
# and the whole repository, `node_modules` included, ends up in the context.
#
# The context is the repository root, so these paths are repo-relative. Keeping
# build output and secrets out of it is what makes the manifest-first COPY
# ordering actually cache.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.next
**/.turbo
.git
.github
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/coverage
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
